---
id: com.example.shogi
name: Shogi
version: 0.1.0
---

A Composer plugin that puts a shogi board in every space, built in a sandbox on EDGE and published to its reader's
private plugin registry, where they install it.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term       | URI                          |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| `type`     | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`  |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Types

```mdl
type Side
  desc: The two players. Sente moves first and sits at the bottom of the board.
  literals: sente | gote
```

```mdl
type PieceKind
  desc: The eight kinds of piece, before promotion.
  literals: king | rook | bishop | gold | silver | knight | lance | pawn
```

```mdl
type Piece
  desc: One piece on the board.
  fields:
    kind: PieceKind
    owner: Side
    promoted: boolean      # false at the start; only rook, bishop, silver, knight, lance and pawn promote
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Board
  desc: A "Shogi" group in each space's navtree with a "Board" page under it, showing the board in the starting position.

  req F-1.1: The page shows 81 squares in nine ranks of nine, files 9 to 1 from left to right and ranks a to i from top to bottom, as a shogi diagram reads.
  req F-1.2: The board opens on the starting position, twenty `type:Piece`s a side: sente's on ranks g to i, gote's on ranks a to c and drawn upside down.
  req F-1.3: Each square carries `data-testid="shogi.square"` and a `data-square` naming it (`7g`); each piece carries `data-testid="shogi.piece"` with its kind and owner as `data-kind` and `data-owner`.
  req F-1.4: The plugin adds to the navtree and never replaces it: no workspace, no rail tab.
```

F-2 to F-4 are named on the project's feature map — Moves, Captures and promotion, Published to the registry — and
are not written yet. Each gets a `feat` block here, with its requirements, before the implementation is planned.
Dropping a captured piece back onto the board is out of scope.

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: The board opens on the starting position
  when: a reader opens Board under the Shogi group of a space
  then: the board holds forty pieces, sente's nine pawns on rank g and gote's king on 5a
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: The Shogi Plugin template seeds this spec partly written, with the project's features filed against it and a partial task list; the assistant completes the spec, plans the implementation as tasks and works them until the plugin is in my private plugin registry.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The seeded spec states the pieces and [F-1] in full and only names F-2 to F-4, which the assistant writes from the feature map; drops are out of scope. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: The board is the part a reader can state up front; the moves, captures and the publish are where the agent's plan has to meet the rules of the game and the plugin toolchain.
  rejected: Including drops, which roughly doubles the move rules for a demo that has to finish in one run.
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

`decision` is defined in [`changelog.mdl`](https://github.com/dxos/dxos/blob/main/packages/reflect/deus/lang/changelog.mdl).
